Z||000000||wantav8||10-03-2001||10:36 PM||||I am dropping a 2.8 out of an 86 in my 84 ferrari/fiero. I know it would be much easier to just carb it than to switch the hole wire harness, Do you think I would loose much power or drivabillity ? I am planning on using a 400 holly and S-10 intake/distributor.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wantav8.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||10-03-2001||11:30 PM||||Depending on what kind of intake you are going to run, you should lose some bottom end power and make more high rpm power. The Fiero tuned port is great for low end torque, but quickly runs out of breath.||||reg||1
